 'Madhu Sriwastav is a Kolkata-based academic, poet, reviewer and translator. Her first poetry collection is Trips Climbs Circles. She translated Chitra Mudgal’s Hindi novel Post Box No. 203, Nala Sopara into English; in her own account of that work, she reflects on carrying its mixed linguistic textures and cultural meanings into another language.',
 'Her Kabita Live poems approach both connection and creation through physical images. Distances follows words that cannot close a silence, moving from slipping fish and open seas towards a dry desert. Creation begins with a seed, then places a painted pot and the artist’s hands beside the larger processes that sustain and end life. One poem tests the reach of language; the other brings making into a posture of humility.'
